<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (Modern radar systems remain a primary means of detecting, tracking, and identifying aerospace vehicles. RCS is strongly dependent on external geometry, orientation, and frequency. Traditional aerospace configurations, designed primarily for aerodynamic, structural, mission requirements, produce geometric features that increase detectability. Stealth technology addresses this through geometric shaping that redirects scattered energy away from the radar receiver.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
